{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrz2QCV1bbMERvSgyHZz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Root cause:** `reporting/dedupe.py` tracked seen event IDs in a list and checked membership with `r.event_id in seen_ids`. A list lookup is linear, so deduplication was O(n²). The commit that introduced the list (the \"refactored to keep insertion order\" change) also made this quadratic. With 30k rows, that is hundreds of millions of comparisons. On this machine, `build_report` over 33k rows took 5.05 s before the fix. Production runs were probably slower because of the bigger data and a different machine, which fits the hour-plus runtime in the ticket.\n\n**Fix** (`reporting/dedupe.py`): `seen_ids` is now a `set`. Output is unchanged because the list still keeps only the first occurrence of each ID in input order. `dedupe_rows`, `build_report`, and the rest of the public API are untouched.\n\n**Regression test** (`tests/test_dedupe.py`, new):\n- `test_dedupe_is_linear_in_rows` counts `__eq__` calls on the event IDs rather than timing the run, so it is not flaky. It fails on the old code (1,999,000 comparisons against a bound of 2,000) and passes on the fix.\n- `test_dedupe_keeps_first_occurrence_order` pins the output order.\n- `test_build_report_large_input_with_retries` checks the totals for 30k rows with retried duplicates.\n\n**Results:**\n- Full suite (`python -m pytest`): 4 passed.\n- Same 33k-row build: 5.05 s before, 0.02 s after.\n\nI did not commit. `git status` also shows the tracked `reporting/__pycache__/dedupe.cpython-314.pyc` as modified, because running pytest regenerated it. You probably want to leave that out of the commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9650,"cache_read_input_tokens":43783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9650},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebdbdafd-64fd-4083-9009-d0181d39f838","uuid":"963df52f-730d-41a8-b37a-5066977069a6","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:32:23.521Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrz2PvNfye4o7fEpM75A"}
